> **Corpus placement** — This standalone document is canonically synthesized in [`B1 — The Derivation Chain`](../../Synthesis Project/B1 — The Derivation Chain.ormd#stage-1-relational-commitment "meta:corresponds_to"). Foundational phenomenological statement of E²: being arises in-between. Canonical treatment in B1 §1.

### Synthesis of Relational Ontology

The document "Our Essence" by Daniel Pace presents a concise philosophical proposition regarding the locus of human identity. It argues against the notion of essence as an isolated, internal property of the individual. Instead, the text asserts that our [essence](#relational-space "ontological:emerges_from") is an emergent phenomenon that [emerges from](#relational-space "ontological:emerges_from") the shared connections between people.

This perspective shifts the focus of being from the "self" to the "relational," suggesting that the [space between us](#relational-space "geometric:embedded_in") is the primary environment in which we are [embedded](#relational-space "geometric:embedded_in"). This [relational space](#relational-space "ontological:defines") serves as the foundational substrate for human existence and meaning.

{#relational-space}